      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the total number of games played in the baseball league, we need to consider the pairs of teams that are playing against each other. Since each team plays three games with each other team, we can calculate the number of games by finding the combinations of pairs. \n\nFor nine teams, the total number of pairs can be found using the combination formula: N(N-1)/2, where N is the number of elements (in this case, the teams). \n\nTo find the number of games played, we need to multiply each pair by 3 (the number of games played in each season). \n\nSo, the total number of games played is: (9(9-1))/2 * 3 = 50\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played in the baseball league is 50.",
